@page "/features"

@* Spec 034 T015 (US1): FR-002 capability areas with real descriptions drawn from README.md.
   Site redesign: alternating media sections built from the real product screenshots in
   wwwroot/img/screenshots (lazy-loaded, explicit width/height to avoid CLS per
   contracts/site-routes.md), followed by the full capability card grid. *@

<PageTitle>Features — AKML SQL</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="The AKML SQL capability set for SQL Server Management Studio 22: schema-aware IntelliSense, a 7-stage formatting pipeline, 130+ static analysis rules, refactoring, snippets, crash-safe SQL history, and schema-grounded AI assistance." />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Features" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Schema-aware IntelliSense, a 7-stage formatting pipeline, 130+ static analysis rules, refactoring, snippets, crash-safe SQL history, and schema-grounded AI assistance." />
</HeadContent>

<div class="page-body container">
    <header class="page-header">
        <p class="eyebrow">Features</p>
        <h1>Everything SQL Prompt did — and then some</h1>
        <p class="page-intro">
            AKML SQL replicates and extends the Redgate SQL Prompt feature set inside SQL Server
            Management Studio 22, powered by a self-contained .NET 10 engine.
        </p>
    </header>

    <section class="media-row" aria-labelledby="media-completion-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">IntelliSense</p>
            <h2 id="media-completion-heading">Find the right JOIN as you type</h2>
            <p>
                Suggestions use your database relationships to bring related tables and their
                ON conditions to the top. See the table, its schema and the join condition
                before you accept it, right inside the SSMS query editor.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="05-join-suggestions" Width="740" Height="476" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Related tables and JOIN conditions"
                           Alt="AKML SQL suggests Northwind tables and their ON conditions after JOIN in the SSMS editor." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row media-row-flip" aria-labelledby="media-wildcard-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">Column selection</p>
            <h2 id="media-wildcard-heading">Turn SELECT * into the columns you need</h2>
            <p>
                Expand a wildcard into an explicit column list. The picker shows data types,
                nullability and key information, with checkboxes so you can choose exactly
                which columns to insert.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="03-expand-wildcard-popup" Width="740" Height="352" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Choose columns before expanding a wildcard"
                           Alt="The AKML SQL wildcard picker lists Northwind Products columns with selection checkboxes, data types and key details." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row" aria-labelledby="media-styles-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">Format styles</p>
            <h2 id="media-styles-heading">Shape your SQL, see every change</h2>
            <p>
                Choose a style, search its options and fine-tune whitespace, casing, lists
                and JOIN layout. A live SQL preview shows the effect of your changes.
                Import and export SQL Prompt styles to keep your team's formatting familiar.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="02-format-styles" Width="1046" Height="673" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Style options alongside a live preview"
                           Alt="The AKML SQL Format styles window with Khamis Style selected, a searchable options tree, JOIN settings and SQL preview." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row media-row-flip" aria-labelledby="media-history-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">SQL History</p>
            <h2 id="media-history-heading">Get back to the query that worked</h2>
            <p>
                Search earlier queries, star the ones you use often and browse them by date.
                Repeated runs stay grouped together, with a SQL preview and saved versions
                ready to reopen in your editor.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="01-sql-history" Width="804" Height="558" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Search, starred queries and SQL preview"
                           Alt="AKML SQL History shows starred Northwind queries grouped under Today and previews a top customers by revenue query." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row" aria-labelledby="media-options-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">Options</p>
            <h2 id="media-options-heading">Make the editor work your way</h2>
            <p>
                Search settings or browse familiar categories for suggestions, inserted code,
                formatting and query tools. Set completion behavior, suggestion limits and
                trigger delay, with descriptions beside the controls.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="11-options" Width="866" Height="613" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Searchable settings for your workflow"
                           Alt="AKML SQL Options on Suggestions, Behavior, showing completion toggles, maximum suggestions and trigger delay." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row media-row-flip" aria-labelledby="media-palette-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">Command palette</p>
            <h2 id="media-palette-heading">Find an action without hunting through menus</h2>
            <p>
                Type what you want to do and jump straight to it. Find formatting commands,
                style editing and SQL transformations in one searchable list, with keyboard
                shortcuts shown alongside the actions.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="10-command-palette" Width="600" Height="400" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="Formatting commands, one search away"
                           Alt="The AKML SQL command palette filtered by format, listing Format Styles, Format SQL Document, Format Selection and related actions." />
    </section>

    <section class="media-row" aria-labelledby="media-safety-heading">
        <div class="media-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">Execution warnings</p>
            <h2 id="media-safety-heading">A moment to check before a risky query</h2>
            <p>
                See a warning when a statement could change every row or when you are about
                to modify a production database. The prompt names the target and explains
                the risk before you decide whether to continue.
            </p>
        </div>
        <ProductScreenshot Name="12-safety-prompt" Width="506" Height="421" Class="media-frame"
                           Caption="An explicit warning before execution"
                           Alt="An AKML SQL execution warning highlights an UPDATE without WHERE against dbo.Products and offers Execute Anyway or Cancel." />
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="capability-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Deep dive</p>
        <h2 id="capability-heading">The full capability set</h2>
        <ul class="card-grid feature-list">
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="intellisense" /></span>
                <h3>IntelliSense</h3>
                <p>
                    Suggestions for columns, aliases, objects, keywords, JOINs (with foreign-key ON
                    conditions), variables, parameters, snippets, databases, and GROUP BY lists, plus
                    Quick Info and signature help — with fuzzy matching, dot-trigger, and schema-aware ranking.
                    The SQL Prompt-style popup shows type-coded icon badges and turns semi-transparent
                    while you hold Ctrl to peek at the code behind it.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="formatting" /></span>
                <h3>Code formatting</h3>
                <p>
                    A 7-stage pipeline (parse → annotate → layout → casing → emit → validate → idempotency)
                    behind Format Document, Format Selection, Bulk Format, and Unformat. Share styles as
                    <code>.akmlstyle</code> profiles, and round-trip SQL Prompt <code>.sqlpromptstylev2</code>
                    XML — import and export — so existing team styles carry over unchanged.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="analysis" /></span>
                <h3>Static analysis</h3>
                <p>
                    More than 130 rules across 8 categories — Performance, Best Practices, Security,
                    Style, Design, Deprecated, Execution, and Naming — with inline suppressions,
                    per-project <code>.casettings</code>, and native SSMS Error List integration.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="refactoring" /></span>
                <h3>Refactoring</h3>
                <p>
                    Smart Rename, Script as ALTER, Inline EXEC, Inline Stored Procedure, Convert INSERT to
                    UPDATE, and Find Invalid Objects, plus light-bulb fixes — expand wildcards, qualify
                    object names, turn sp_executesql into static SQL, surround with BEGIN/END — that
                    reshape SQL in a single action.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="snippets" /></span>
                <h3>Snippets</h3>
                <p>
                    Personal, team, and built-in snippet folders with context-aware filtering, so the
                    right snippet surfaces where it applies. A surround-with chord wraps a selection in
                    blocks like transactions or try/catch.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="history" /></span>
                <h3>SQL History</h3>
                <p>
                    A full, crash-safe history of every executed query in a three-panel UI — queries,
                    versions, and a syntax-highlighted preview — with full-text search and star,
                    open, and closed filters.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li class="card feature-card">
                <span class="feature-card-icon" aria-hidden="true"><FeatureIcon Name="ai" /></span>
                <h3>AI assistance</h3>
                <p>
                    Explain, Fix, Chat, and Ghost Text inline autocomplete in SSMS, plus Text-to-SQL,
                    Optimize, and Index Analysis in the web edition — all schema-aware, so suggestions
                    are grounded in the database you are actually working against.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <p class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/download">Download AKML SQL</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/docs">Read the docs</a>
    </p>
</div>
